const e={id:"node-os-process",title:{en:"OS, Process & Environment Variables",hi:"OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env)"},difficulty:"Beginner",readTime:8,sections:[{type:"concept",heading:{en:"1. The os Module and the Global process Object",hi:"1. os Module Aur Global process Object Kya Hain?"},body:{en:"When building backend applications, your code does not run in a vacuum—it runs on an operating system with specific CPU cores, RAM limits, and environment configurations.\n\nNode.js gives you two essential utilities to inspect and interact with the host system:\n1. **The `node:os` Module**:\n   - Provides direct access to operating system hardware details.\n   - Inspect CPU cores (`os.cpus()`), available RAM (`os.freemem()`), system uptime, and platform architecture.\n2. **The Global `process` Object**:\n   - A global object available everywhere without requiring an `import`.\n   - Represents the currently running Node.js runtime process.\n   - Access environment variables (`process.env`), command-line arguments (`process.argv`), process ID (`process.pid`), and control lifecycle shutdown (`process.exit()`).",hi:"Backend apps kisi hawa mein nahi chalti—wo physical ya cloud servers par chalti hain jahan specific CPU, RAM aur operating system hota hai.\n\nNode.js humein system se baat karne ke liye do tools deta hai:\n1. **`node:os` Module**:\n   - Server ke hardware ki jankari nikalta hai.\n   - Kitne CPU cores hain (`os.cpus()`), kitni RAM khali hai (`os.freemem()`), aur OS kaunsa hai.\n2. **Global `process` Object**:\n   - Ek global object jise `import` karne ki zaroorat nahi hoti.\n   - Yeh chalte hue current Node program ko represent karta hai.\n   - Isse secret environment variables (`process.env`), terminal arguments (`process.argv`), process ID (`process.pid`), aur app ko band karna (`process.exit()`) control hota hai."}},{type:"concept",heading:{en:"2. Environment Variables & Secure Configuration",hi:"2. Environment Variables Aur Secret Security (process.env)"},body:{en:"**Rule #1 of Backend Development: NEVER hardcode secret credentials in your source code!**\n\nDatabase passwords, JWT secret tokens, and payment gateway keys must never be committed to Git. If you push code with API keys to GitHub, automated bots can scrape your credentials in under 60 seconds!\n\n### The Solution: `process.env` & `.env`\n- Secret keys are stored in a local `.env` file on your machine.\n- The `.env` file is added to **`.gitignore`**.\n- A package like **`dotenv`** (or modern Node `--env-file=.env`) loads these variables into `process.env` at application startup.\n- In production (Render, Vercel, AWS), environment variables are configured securely through the cloud provider's dashboard.",hi:"**Backend Development Ka Pehla Niyam: Kabhi bhi secrets aur passwords ko source code mein hardcode na karein!**\n\nDatabase connection strings, JWT secret keys, aur Stripe/Razorpay keys ko code mein likhkar Git par push karne se automated bots 1 minute ke andar aapke account ko hack kar sakte hain!\n\n### Solution: `process.env` Aur `.env`\n- Saare secrets ko project ke root par `.env` file mein rakha jata hai.\n- `.env` file ko **`.gitignore`** mein daala jata hai taaki wo GitHub par na jaye.\n- App start hote waqt `dotenv` ya Node ka naya flag `node --env-file=.env app.js` in values ko `process.env` mein load kar deta hai.\n- Production servers (jaise Render ya AWS) par ye variables cloud dashboard ki settings se inject kiye jaate hain."}},{type:"analogy",heading:{en:"Real-Life Analogy: The Factory Cockpit & Secret Manager Locker",hi:"Real-Life Analogy: Factory Ka Control Room Aur Manager Ka Secret Locker"},body:{en:"Imagine running a large **Automobile Manufacturing Plant**:\n\n- **The `os` Module is the Factory Gauge Panel**:\n  - The digital display shows 8 active power generators (`os.cpus().length = 8`) and 16 GB of diesel remaining in the reserve tank (`os.freemem()`).\n  - If fuel is critically low, the engineer throttles down production.\n- **The `process` Object is the Factory Main Power Switch**:\n  - The red emergency button stops the entire assembly line: `process.exit(1)`.\n  - The process ID tag on the wall confirms this is Plant Unit #4029 (`process.pid`).\n- **`process.env` is the Manager's Private Wallet**:\n  - The factory vault combination code is kept in the manager's pocket notebook (`.env`). It is NOT painted on the factory signboard for every visitor to read!",hi:"Sochiye ek badi **Car Factory Ka Control Room**:\n\n- **`os` Module Digital Meter Jaisa Hai**:\n  - Yeh batata hai ki factory mein kitne engine chal rahe hain (`os.cpus().length = 8`) aur generator mein kitna diesel bacha hai (`os.freemem()`).\n  - Agar system mein load zyada ho toh alert generate hota hai.\n- **`process` Main Power Switch Jaisa Hai**:\n  - Emergency lever kheenchte hi poori factory turant band ho jaati hai (`process.exit(1)`).\n  - Har chalte hue unit ka apna badge number hota hai (`process.pid`).\n- **`process.env` Manager Ka Private Vault Hai**:\n  - Locker ki chabi aur password manager ki jeb mein rehta hai (`.env`). Wo factory ke main gate par poster laga kar nahi likha jata!"}},{type:"syntax",heading:{en:"4. Syntax: os, process.env & Command-Line Arguments",hi:"4. Syntax: os, process.env Aur process.argv"},body:{en:`\`\`\`javascript
import os from 'node:os';

// 1. Hardware Inspection
const totalMemGB = (os.totalmem() / 1024 ** 3).toFixed(1);
const freeMemGB = (os.freemem() / 1024 ** 3).toFixed(1);
const numCores = os.cpus().length;

// 2. Reading Environment Variables with Safe Defaults
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 5000;
const NODE_ENV = process.env.NODE_ENV || 'development';
const MONGO_URI = process.env.MONGO_URI;

// 3. Command Line Arguments (process.argv)
// node server.js --port=8080 --mode=cluster
// process.argv[0] -> path to node executable
// process.argv[1] -> path to running script
// process.argv[2] -> '--port=8080'
\`\`\``,hi:`\`\`\`javascript
import os from 'node:os';

// 1. System Memory & CPU Check
const freeRAM = (os.freemem() / (1024 * 1024 * 1024)).toFixed(2);
const cpuCount = os.cpus().length;

// 2. Environment Variables Read Karna (Safe Fallback Ke Saath)
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 5000;
const DB_URL = process.env.DATABASE_URL;

// 3. Terminal Arguments Parse Karna
// Agar command hai: node app.js --port 3000
// process.argv[0] = node binary
// process.argv[1] = file path
// process.argv[2] = '--port'
\`\`\``}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"5. Practical Examples: Server Health, CLI Parser & Graceful Shutdown",hi:"5. Practical Examples: Server Health, CLI Parser aur Graceful Shutdown"},body:{en:`### Example 1: Server Hardware & Health Metric Reporter
A lightweight health inspection script reporting memory usage, CPU model, and system uptime.`,hi:`### Example 1: Server Health & Resource Monitoring Utility
System memory, CPU details aur server uptime calculate karne ka clean script.`},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"systemHealth.js",snippet:`// Example 1: System Hardware Metrics with node:os
import os from "node:os";

function getSystemHealthMetrics() {
  const totalBytes = os.totalmem();
  const freeBytes = os.freemem();
  const usedBytes = totalBytes - freeBytes;
  const memoryUsagePercent = ((usedBytes / totalBytes) * 100).toFixed(1);

  const cpus = os.cpus();
  const uptimeHours = (os.uptime() / 3600).toFixed(1);

  return {
    osPlatform: \`\${os.type()} (\${os.platform()} \${os.arch()})\`,
    cpuModel: cpus[0]?.model || "Generic CPU",
    cpuCores: cpus.length,
    systemUptime: \`\${uptimeHours} hours\`,
    memory: {
      total: \`\${(totalBytes / 1024 ** 3).toFixed(2)} GB\`,
      free: \`\${(freeBytes / 1024 ** 3).toFixed(2)} GB\`,
      usagePercentage: \`\${memoryUsagePercent}%\`
    },
    processId: process.pid,
    nodeVersion: process.version
  };
}

console.log("=== SERVER TELEMETRY REPORT ===");
console.log(JSON.stringify(getSystemHealthMetrics(), null, 2));`}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 2: Custom Command-Line Argument Parser",hi:"Example 2: process.argv Se Custom CLI Flag Parser Banana"},body:{en:"### Example 2: Parsing Custom Flags (`--port=8000 --env=prod`)\nHow to extract key-value flags from `process.argv` without third-party dependencies.",hi:`### Example 2: Terminal Flags Ko Parse Karna
Bina kisi external library ke terminal arguments se values nikalna.`},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"cliParser.js",snippet:`// Example 2: Native CLI Argument Parser
function parseCommandLineArgs() {
  // Slice off the first 2 default entries (node executable and file path)
  const rawArgs = process.argv.slice(2);
  const parsed = {};

  rawArgs.forEach((arg) => {
    if (arg.startsWith("--")) {
      const [key, value] = arg.slice(2).split("=");
      parsed[key] = value !== undefined ? value : true;
    }
  });

  return parsed;
}

// Simulated execution: node server.js --port=4000 --env=production --cluster
const config = parseCommandLineArgs();
console.log("Parsed CLI Configuration:", config);

const port = config.port || 3000;
const environment = config.env || "development";
console.log(\`Starting server on port \${port} in \${environment} mode...\`);`}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 3: Enterprise Graceful Shutdown on SIGINT and SIGTERM",hi:"Example 3: Production Graceful Shutdown (SIGINT / SIGTERM)"},body:{en:"### Example 3: Handling Process Termination Signals\nWhen deploying on cloud platforms (Docker, Kubernetes, Render), the host sends a `SIGTERM` signal before shutting down. Graceful shutdown ensures active HTTP requests finish and database connections close cleanly!",hi:`### Example 3: Server Ko Safely Band Karna (Graceful Shutdown)
Production mein server restart ya deploy hote waqt database connections safely close karna taaki data corrupt na ho.`},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"gracefulShutdown.js",snippet:`// Example 3: Production Graceful Shutdown Pattern
import http from "node:http";

const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {
  res.writeHead(200, { "Content-Type": "text/plain" });
  res.end("Hello from production server!");
});

const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;
server.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(\`Server online on port \${PORT} [PID: \${process.pid}]\`);
});

// Mock database connection pool
const mockDbPool = {
  close: async () => {
    console.log("Closing active MongoDB connection pool...");
    await new Promise((res) => setTimeout(res, 500));
    console.log("MongoDB connection closed cleanly.");
  }
};

// Graceful shutdown handler
async function handleShutdown(signal) {
  console.log(\`\\nReceived \${signal}. Initiating graceful termination sequence...\`);

  // 1. Stop accepting new incoming HTTP connections
  server.close(async () => {
    console.log("HTTP server closed. No new connections accepted.");

    // 2. Close database pools
    try {
      await mockDbPool.close();
      console.log("All cleanup complete. Exiting process safely.");
      process.exit(0); // Exit with success code 0
    } catch (err) {
      console.error("Error during cleanup:", err);
      process.exit(1); // Exit with error code 1
    }
  });

  // 3. Force shutdown if cleanup hangs past 10 seconds
  setTimeout(() => {
    console.error("Could not close connections in time, forcefully shutting down!");
    process.exit(1);
  }, 10000).unref(); // .unref allows Node to exit if nothing else is pending
}

// Listen for termination signals
process.on("SIGTERM", () => handleShutdown("SIGTERM")); // From cloud provider / Docker
process.on("SIGINT", () => handleShutdown("SIGINT"));   // From Ctrl+C in terminal`}},{type:"mistakes",heading:{en:"6. Common Mistakes with OS & Process",hi:"6. Process Aur Environment Variables Ki Badi Galtiyan"},mistakes:[{mistake:{en:"Committing the .env file containing API secrets directly into the Git repository.",hi:"Passwords aur secret keys wali `.env` file ko Git repo mein commit kar dena."},correction:{en:"Always list `.env` in `.gitignore`. Create a sanitized `.env.example` file with dummy values for other developers on the team to copy.",hi:"Hamesha `.gitignore` mein `.env` likhein. Team ke liye dummy values wali `.env.example` file banayein."},code:`# .gitignore
.env
.env.local

# .env.example (Safe to commit)
PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@cluster.mongodb.net/dbname
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret_here`},{mistake:{en:"Calling `process.exit(0)` immediately while asynchronous tasks or database writes are still pending.",hi:"Pending database writes complete hone se pehle turant `process.exit(0)` call kar dena."},correction:{en:"`process.exit()` terminates the runtime process instantly, aborting any pending I/O or network packets. Always wait for database connections and HTTP servers to close gracefully first.",hi:"`process.exit()` bina kisi wait ke turant process kill kar deta hai. Hamesha pehle `server.close()` aur database close ka intezar karein."},code:`// BAD (Data corruption risk):
// process.exit(0);

// GOOD:
// await db.close();
// server.close(() => process.exit(0));`}]},{type:"summary",heading:{en:"7. Production Best Practices",hi:"7. Production Best Practices"},body:{en:"- **Native `--env-file` (Node 20+)**: Modern Node natively supports loading env files without third-party packages: `node --env-file=.env server.js`.\n- **Always Validate Envs on Startup**: Validate that required variables (`MONGO_URI`, `JWT_SECRET`) are present during bootup. If missing, fail fast with a descriptive error before serving requests.\n- **Listen for Uncaught Exceptions**: Attach `process.on('unhandledRejection')` and `process.on('uncaughtException')` to log critical failures before shutting down.",hi:"- **Node 20+ Native Env**: Naye Node versions mein bina dotenv ke direct `node --env-file=.env server.js` chala sakte hain.\n- **Startup Par Check Karein**: Server start hote hi verify karein ki saari zaroori keys (`JWT_SECRET`, `MONGO_URI`) maujood hain ya nahi.\n- **Crash Loggers**: `process.on('unhandledRejection')` lagakar unhandled promise errors ko track karein."}},{type:"interview",heading:{en:"8. Top Interview Questions & Answers",hi:"8. Top Interview Sawal Aur Jawab"},questions:[{q:{en:"What is the difference between process.env and process.argv?",hi:"process.env aur process.argv mein kya antar hota hai?"},a:{en:"process.env is a key-value object containing the environment variables of the host machine (e.g. PORT, NODE_ENV, secret tokens). process.argv is an array containing the command-line arguments passed when the Node process was launched (e.g. ['node', 'server.js', '--port=8080']).",hi:"process.env ek object hai jismein server ke environment variables aur secret keys (jaise PORT, DATABASE_URL) store hote hain. process.argv ek array hai jismein terminal se pass kiye gaye command-line arguments hote hain."}},{q:{en:"What is Graceful Shutdown and why is it important?",hi:"Graceful Shutdown kya hota hai aur yeh zaroori kyun hai?"},a:{en:"Graceful shutdown is the process of safely stopping a web server when receiving a termination signal (SIGTERM/SIGINT). Instead of abruptly killing the process, the server stops accepting new connections, allows in-flight HTTP requests to complete, closes database connection pools, flushes file logs, and then cleanly exits with code 0. This prevents data corruption during deployments.",hi:"Graceful shutdown ka matlab hai server ko bina data loss ke safely band karna. Jab host system SIGTERM bhejta hai, toh server naye users ko rok deta hai, purane chal rahe orders/requests ko poora hone deta hai, database connections close karta hai aur fir exit hota hai. Isse users ka data corrupt nahi hota."}},{q:{en:"How does the `os.cpus()` method help in scaling Node.js applications?",hi:"`os.cpus()` method Node.js apps ko scale karne mein kaise madad karta hai?"},a:{en:"Because Node.js runs single-threaded on one core, a server with 8 CPU cores would only utilize 12.5% of its compute power with a single Node instance. By querying `os.cpus().length`, tools like the Node `cluster` module or PM2 can automatically spawn one worker process per CPU core, maximizing server throughput.",hi:"Kyunki Node.js single thread par chalta hai, 8 CPU core wale server par ek aam Node app sirf 1 core use kar pati hai. `os.cpus().length` se pata karke hum `cluster` module ya PM2 se har CPU core ke liye 1 process spawn kar sakte hain, jisse server ki capacity 8 guna badh jaati hai."}}]},{type:"summary",heading:{en:"9. Summary Cheatsheet",hi:"9. Summary Cheatsheet"},body:{en:"- **node:os**: `os.cpus()`, `os.totalmem()`, `os.freemem()`, `os.platform()`.\n- **process.env**: Environment variables; keep secrets in `.env`.\n- **process.argv**: Array of command-line arguments.\n- **process.pid**: Current OS process identifier.\n- **Graceful Shutdown**: Intercept `SIGTERM` / `SIGINT` to close database pools before exit.",hi:"- **os**: Hardware metrics (CPUs, RAM, Platform).\n- **process.env**: Secrets aur configurations (Git mein na daalein).\n- **process.argv**: Terminal flags ka array.\n- **Shutdown**: `SIGINT` aur `SIGTERM` sunkar database safely close karein."}}],quiz:[{q:{en:"Which global object provides access to environment variables in Node.js?",hi:"Node.js mein environment variables access karne ke liye kaunsa global object use hota hai?"},options:[{en:"process.env",hi:"process.env"},{en:"os.environment",hi:"os.environment"},{en:"window.env",hi:"window.env"},{en:"global.variables",hi:"global.variables"}],answerIndex:0,explanation:{en:"process.env is the standard global object storing user and host environment variables.",hi:"process.env standard global object hai jismein environment variables hote hain."}},{q:{en:"What is stored at index 0 and index 1 of the `process.argv` array?",hi:"`process.argv` array ke index 0 aur index 1 par kya store hota hai?"},options:[{en:"Index 0 is the path to the node binary; Index 1 is the path to the executed script file",hi:"Index 0 node binary ka path hota hai; Index 1 chalne wali script file ka path hota hai"},{en:"Index 0 is the port; Index 1 is the host",hi:"Index 0 port hota hai; Index 1 host hota hai"},{en:"Index 0 is the username; Index 1 is the password",hi:"Index 0 username hota hai; Index 1 password hota hai"},{en:"They are always empty strings",hi:"Wo hamesha empty strings hote hain"}],answerIndex:0,explanation:{en:"process.argv[0] is the absolute path to node, and process.argv[1] is the path to the script being run. Custom CLI arguments begin at index 2.",hi:"Index 0 par Node executable ka path aur Index 1 par script ka path hota hai. Custom arguments index 2 se start hote hain."}},{q:{en:"Which operating system signal is typically sent by cloud platforms (Docker, Kubernetes) to request a graceful shutdown?",hi:"Cloud platforms (Docker, Kubernetes) graceful shutdown request karne ke liye kaunsa OS signal bhejte hain?"},options:[{en:"SIGTERM",hi:"SIGTERM"},{en:"SIGKILL",hi:"SIGKILL"},{en:"SIGSTOP",hi:"SIGSTOP"},{en:"SIGPAUSE",hi:"SIGPAUSE"}],answerIndex:0,explanation:{en:"SIGTERM is the standard termination signal asking the process to clean up and exit. SIGKILL forcefully kills the process without allowing cleanup.",hi:"SIGTERM termination signal bhejta hai jo app ko cleanup karne ka mauka deta hai. SIGKILL bina kisi cleanup ke zabardasti kill karta hai."}},{question:{en:"What is the core architectural purpose of OS, Process & Environment Variables in the modern full-stack MERN ecosystem?",hi:"Modern full-stack MERN ecosystem mein OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) ka mukhya architectural maksad kya hota hai?"},options:[{en:"It manages physical computer cooling and power supply",hi:"Ye physical computer cooling aur power supply manage karta hai"},{en:"It provides structured, robust, and scalable patterns for handling os, process & environment variables with high performance and maintainability",hi:"Ye high performance aur maintainability ke saath OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) ko handle karne ka structured aur scalable pattern provide karta hai"},{en:"It completely replaces JavaScript with binary machine code in browser tabs",hi:"Ye browser tabs mein JavaScript ko binary machine code se replace karta hai"},{en:"It is only used for printing documents to physical printers",hi:"Ye sirf physical printers par documents print karne ke liye hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"OS, Process & Environment Variables establishes clean separation of concerns, ensuring predictable data flow, robust error handling, and optimal runtime performance in production.",hi:"OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) clean architecture aur separation of concerns deta hai jisse application scalable aur maintainable banti hai."}},{question:{en:"What critical development bottleneck or anti-pattern does OS, Process & Environment Variables directly resolve?",hi:"OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) kis critical development bottleneck ya anti-pattern ko seedhe solve karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It replaces chaotic, tightly coupled ad-hoc logic with declarative, predictable control flow and structured data contracts",hi:"Ye chaotic aur tightly coupled logic ko hata kar declarative, predictable flow aur structured data contracts deta hai"},{en:"It forces the operating system to shut down when errors occur",hi:"Error aane par ye operating system band kar deta hai"},{en:"It deletes all database records older than 24 hours automatically",hi:"Ye 24 ghante purane DB records delete karta hai"},{en:"It blocks all outgoing HTTP network requests to conserve bandwidth",hi:"Ye bandwidth bachane ke liye network requests block karta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Without OS, Process & Environment Variables, applications suffer from brittle code, maintenance overhead, and unhandled edge cases that manifest as production crashes.",hi:"OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) ke bina code brittle ho jata hai aur production mein unexpected errors aate hain."}},{question:{en:"When reasoning about OS, Process & Environment Variables, how is its mental model best conceptualized through real-world analogies?",hi:"OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) ko real-world analogies ke zariye kaise best samjha ja sakta hai?"},options:[{en:"As a completely offline computer with zero network or database connections",hi:"Ek offline computer ki tarah jisme koi connection na ho"},{en:"As a disciplined, coordinated workflow where inputs are validated and processed through standardized checkpoints rather than ad-hoc handling",hi:"Ek disciplined workflow ki tarah jahan data ko structured checkpoints ke zariye step-by-step process kiya jata hai"},{en:"As a random number generator with non-deterministic output",hi:"Random number generator ki tarah jiska koi niyam na ho"},{en:"As a static text document that cannot be modified or read",hi:"Static text document jo padha na ja sake"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Real-world workflow analogies help engineers visualize component boundaries, request lifecycles, and data transformations intuitively.",hi:"Real-world analogies component boundaries aur request lifecycle ko visual aur intuitive banati hain."}},{question:{en:"When declaring and implementing OS, Process & Environment Variables, what syntactic convention is essential to prevent runtime errors?",hi:"OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) ko declare aur implement karte waqt kaunsa syntax niyam runtime errors rokne ke liye zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Adhering strictly to required parameters, handling asynchronous promises/callbacks cleanly, and verifying return value types",hi:"Zaroori parameters sahi pass karna, async promises ko handle karna aur return value types verify karna"},{en:"Wrapping every line of code inside an eval() execution block",hi:"Har line ko eval() block mein wrap karna"},{en:"Omitting import and require statements to reduce file size",hi:"File size ghatane ke liye import statements hatana"},{en:"Writing all code on a single continuous line without whitespace",hi:"Bina whitespace ke single line par code likhna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Following standard ES6+ syntax contracts and properly handling promise resolution ensures execution safety and eliminates TypeError exceptions.",hi:"ES6+ syntax aur promise handling ke standard rules follow karne se TypeError aur crashes nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"What is a common pitfall developers encounter when working with OS, Process & Environment Variables?",hi:"OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) ke saath kaam karte waqt developers aksar kaunsi aam galati karte hain?"},options:[{en:"Writing unit tests before implementing features",hi:"Feature likhne se pehle unit tests likhna"},{en:"Failing to handle failure edge cases, mutating shared state directly, or neglecting defensive validation guard clauses",hi:"Failure edge cases ko handle na karna, shared state direct mutate karna ya validation guard clauses na lagana"},{en:"Using strict equality checks (===) instead of loose equality (==)",hi:"Loose equality ke badle strict equality use karna"},{en:"Writing clear inline code documentation",hi:"Clear inline code comments likhna"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Neglecting edge cases and error handling causes silent regressions and race conditions that surface under concurrent user workloads.",hi:"Edge cases aur error handling miss karne se high-traffic production load mein silent bugs paida hote hain."}},{question:{en:"According to production best practices, how should OS, Process & Environment Variables be architected for enterprise-grade stability?",hi:"Production best practices ke mutabiq enterprise-grade stability ke liye OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) ko kaise architect karna chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Enforce modular boundaries, validate all incoming payloads against schemas, log structured context, and maintain pure functions where possible",hi:"Modular boundaries enforce karein, payloads ko schema se validate karein, structured logs rakhein aur pure functions use karein"},{en:"Hardcode sensitive database connection strings directly in client-side files",hi:"Database passwords ko client files mein hardcode karna"},{en:"Disable all linter rules and type warnings globally",hi:"Linter aur type warnings ko globally disable karna"},{en:"Store all user session variables in global un-scoped memory arrays",hi:"Global memory arrays mein sessions store karna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Enterprise-grade code prioritizes modularity, strict input validation, structured observability, and stateless designs.",hi:"Production hardening ke liye modular code, schema validation aur observability standard rules hote hain."}},{question:{en:"How does proper optimization of OS, Process & Environment Variables impact application memory and CPU consumption?",hi:"OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) ko sahi dhang se optimize karne par application memory aur CPU par kya asar padta hai?"},options:[{en:"It increases server CPU temperature to 100 degrees Celsius",hi:"Server CPU temperature 100 degrees kar deta hai"},{en:"It minimizes redundant computations, eliminates memory leaks from uncleaned references, and maintains low latency under high concurrency",hi:"Ye redundant computations ghatata hai, memory leaks khatam karta hai aur high concurrency mein low latency maintain karta hai"},{en:"It doubles heap RAM allocation unconditionally",hi:"Heap RAM ko zabardasti double karta hai"},{en:"Optimization has zero measurable impact in modern web engines",hi:"Modern web engines par optimization ka koi asar nahi hota"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Preventing unnecessary allocations and cleaning up resources ensures low garbage collection pressure and predictable response times.",hi:"Memory leak rokne aur unnecessary allocations hatane se Garbage Collector par load kam rehta hai aur response fast rehta hai."}},{question:{en:"What security principle is non-negotiable when handling data within OS, Process & Environment Variables?",hi:"OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) mein data handle karte waqt kaunsa security principle non-negotiable hota hai?"},options:[{en:"Never trust client-supplied input: always sanitize, authenticate, authorize, and validate against strict schemas on the server",hi:"Client data par blind trust na karein: server par hamesha sanitize, authenticate, authorize aur validate karein"},{en:"Trust all requests coming from mobile devices or web browsers blindly",hi:"Mobile ya browser se aane wali requests par blind trust karein"},{en:"Disable HTTPS and SSL certificates to maximize raw network throughput",hi:"Network throughput ke liye HTTPS band karein"},{en:"Expose database admin credentials to all registered users",hi:"Database admin credentials sabhi users ko expose karein"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Zero-Trust security dictates that every incoming request and data mutation must be validated and authenticated server-side before processing.",hi:"Zero-Trust security ke mutabiq har incoming mutation ko server par strictly validate aur authenticate kiya jana chahiye."}},{question:{en:"How does asynchronous non-blocking execution operate in OS, Process & Environment Variables?",hi:"OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) mein asynchronous non-blocking execution kaise kaam karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It freezes the entire operating system until each operation completes",hi:"Har operation complete hone tak operating system freeze rehta hai"},{en:"I/O operations return Promises or accept callbacks, delegating work to background threads/queues while the main thread remains free to handle incoming tasks",hi:"I/O operations Promises return karte hain aur background queues use karke main thread ko baaki requests ke liye free rakhte hain"},{en:"Async operations execute in reverse alphabetical order automatically",hi:"Async operations reverse alphabetical order mein chalte hain"},{en:"Async code only executes when triggered manually by a user click",hi:"Sirf manual user click par async code chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Non-blocking asynchronous operations resolve via microtasks or event loop queues, ensuring the runtime thread serves concurrent requests smoothly.",hi:"Non-blocking model main thread ko free rakhta hai taaki server bina rukaawat ke multiple users ko simultaneously serve kar sake."}},{question:{en:"What is the recommended pattern for propagating errors that occur in OS, Process & Environment Variables?",hi:"OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) mein error aane par unhe propagate karne ka recommended pattern kya hai?"},options:[{en:"Intercepting the error, enriching it with operational context, and delegating to a centralized error handler or error boundary",hi:"Error ko intercept karna, debug context add karna, aur centralized error handler ya error boundary ko pass karna"},{en:"Swallowing errors silently with empty catch {} blocks to hide problems from logs",hi:"Khaali catch {} blocks se errors ko silently daba dena taaki logs mein na dikhein"},{en:"Shutting down the server machine power immediately",hi:"Server machine power turant band kar dena"},{en:"Sending internal raw stack traces and database credentials to end-user browsers",hi:"Raw stack trace aur DB passwords browser par bhej dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Centralized error propagation provides complete operational observability while shielding internal infrastructure details from end users.",hi:"Centralized error handling se system mein transparency rehti hai aur user ko clean, safe error messages milte hain."}},{question:{en:"When authoring unit or integration tests for OS, Process & Environment Variables, what must the test suite assert?",hi:"OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) ke liye automated tests likhte waqt test suite ko kya assert karna zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Only that the JavaScript file can be saved to disk",hi:"Sirf ye ki file disk par save ho sake"},{en:"Both the happy path (expected inputs producing valid outputs) AND boundary edge cases (null, empty arrays, network timeouts, invalid types)",hi:"Happy path (valid data) AUR boundary edge cases (null, empty array, network timeout, invalid types) dono ko verify karna"},{en:"That the test suite takes at least 24 hours to finish running",hi:"Test suite ko 24 ghante chalna chahiye"},{en:"Testing is considered unnecessary in modern full-stack development",hi:"Modern development mein testing zaroori nahi hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Robust automated test suites verify both standard valid scenarios and defensive failure modes to prevent regressions during deployments.",hi:"Achhi testing valid inputs aur failure states dono ko assert karti hai taaki production deployments safe rahein."}},{question:{en:"How does modular design enhance code maintainability in OS, Process & Environment Variables?",hi:"Modular design OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) mein code maintainability ko kaise badhata hai?"},options:[{en:"By isolating distinct responsibilities into small, reusable, and independently testable units following the Single Responsibility Principle",hi:"Single Responsibility Principle ke zariye alag-alag kaamo ko chote, reusable aur testable units mein baant kar"},{en:"By combining all frontend, backend, and database code into a single 50,000-line script",hi:"Saara code ek hi 50,000-line script mein daal kar"},{en:"By removing all function names and replacing them with random numbers",hi:"Function names hata kar random numbers likhna"},{en:"By forbidding code comments and documentation across the repository",hi:"Comments aur documentation ban kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Modularity reduces cognitive load, simplifies debugging, prevents ripple effects during changes, and enables seamless team collaboration.",hi:"Modular code se readability badhti hai, debugging aasan hoti hai aur ek jagah badlav karne par doosri jagah bugs nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"When application traffic scales 100x, how should OS, Process & Environment Variables be architected to support horizontal scaling?",hi:"Traffic 100x badhne par OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) ko horizontally scale karne ke liye kya design approach honi chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Ensure the component/service is completely stateless, offload shared session/state to Redis/MongoDB, and distribute traffic via a load balancer",hi:"Service ko completely stateless banayein, shared state ko Redis/DB par shift karein aur load balancer se traffic distribute karein"},{en:"Store all user session variables in local in-memory JavaScript objects on the web server",hi:"Server ki local RAM mein session variables store karna"},{en:"Reboot the production server manually whenever memory usage exceeds 10%",hi:"Memory 10% cross hote hi server manually reboot karna"},{en:"Block 95% of incoming users using firewall rules",hi:"95% users ko firewall se block kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Stateless service architecture guarantees that any container instance can handle any incoming request, enabling dynamic auto-scaling without session loss.",hi:"Stateless architecture auto-scaling ka base hai jahan naye containers bina session loss ke instant traffic handle kar sakte hain."}},{question:{en:"In the full-stack MERN paradigm, where does OS, Process & Environment Variables properly belong and execute?",hi:"Full-stack MERN architecture mein OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) kahan belong karta hai aur kahan execute hota hai?"},options:[{en:"In its designated architectural tier (Client browser UI, Express API backend, or MongoDB database) with clean API contracts connecting them",hi:"Apne designated tier (Browser UI, Express API backend, ya MongoDB) mein clean API contracts ke saath"},{en:"Directly on the end-user's local router firmware",hi:"User ke local router firmware par"},{en:"Inside the computer motherboard BIOS chip",hi:"Motherboard BIOS chip mein"},{en:"All MERN code runs strictly inside the MongoDB database engine",hi:"Saara MERN code sirf MongoDB ke andar chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Maintaining clear structural boundaries between client rendering, backend orchestration, and database persistence is the defining trait of MERN.",hi:"Client UI, backend server aur database ke beech saaf boundary maintain karna MERN architecture ka mukhya niyam hai."}},{question:{en:"What telemetry metric or observability signal is most crucial for diagnosing issues with OS, Process & Environment Variables in production?",hi:"Production mein OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) ki problems diagnose karne ke liye sabse zaroori telemetry metric kaunsi hoti hai?"},options:[{en:"The desktop monitor brightness setting of the client",hi:"Client ke monitor ki brightness"},{en:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (HTTP 4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), and heap memory allocation deltas",hi:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), aur heap memory allocation deltas"},{en:"The number of files in the project's root folder",hi:"Root folder mein files ki sankhya"},{en:"The physical keyboard model used by the engineer",hi:"Engineer ke keyboard ka model"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Observability platforms monitor p95/p99 latencies, error frequencies, and memory utilization to identify bottlenecks and regressions early.",hi:"p95/p99 latencies aur error rates monitor karne se crashes aane se pehle hi bottlenecks pakad mein aa jaate hain."}},{question:{en:"Why is eliminating unintended side effects essential when authoring logic for OS, Process & Environment Variables?",hi:"OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) ka logic likhte waqt unintended side effects ko khatam karna kyun zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Side effects introduce unpredictability, corrupt shared state, cause race conditions, and make concurrent code nearly impossible to debug",hi:"Side effects se code unpredictable banta hai, shared state corrupt hoti hai aur race conditions create hoti hain"},{en:"Side effects permanently erase the developer's Git commit history",hi:"Git history permanently delete ho jaati hai"},{en:"Side effects are strictly required by the JavaScript ECMAScript standard",hi:"ECMAScript mein side effects required hain"},{en:"Side effects make all algorithms execute in O(1) time",hi:"Saare algorithms O(1) time mein chalte hain"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Pure and predictable logic produces the same output for identical inputs, guaranteeing thread safety, easy caching, and high reliability.",hi:"Pure logic se shared state safe rehti hai aur same input par hamesha consistent aur predictable output milta hai."}},{question:{en:"How should client-side state be kept in sync with backend server mutations in OS, Process & Environment Variables?",hi:"OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) mein client-side state aur backend server data ko sync mein kaise rakha jata hai?"},options:[{en:"By forcing a complete hard page refresh every 3 seconds",hi:"Har 3 second mein poora page hard refresh karke"},{en:"Using optimistic UI updates with error rollback, automated query cache invalidation (TanStack Query/RTK), or WebSocket change streams",hi:"Optimistic UI updates with rollback, automated query cache invalidation ya WebSocket push streams use karke"},{en:"By disabling all database update operations permanently",hi:"Database updates ko permanently band karke"},{en:"By saving user state in local CSV files on the server desktop",hi:"Server desktop par CSV files save karke"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Modern full-stack architectures synchronize state seamlessly using query cache invalidation, optimistic updates, and real-time socket events.",hi:"Modern apps cache invalidation aur optimistic UI use karti hain taaki UI bina screen reload ke instantly updated rahe."}},{question:{en:"Why is thorough resource cleanup (clearing timers, closing sockets, aborting in-flight requests) critical in OS, Process & Environment Variables?",hi:"OS, Process & Environment Variables (process.env) mein resource cleanup (timers clear karna, sockets band karna, network abort karna) kyun zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"To prevent memory leaks where unreachable or orphaned objects remain retained in heap memory, causing gradual performance degradation and crashes",hi:"Memory leaks rokne ke liye taaki unneeded objects RAM mein jama na hon aur server crash na ho"},{en:"To delete the client's local disk partition",hi:"Client ka local disk partition delete karne ke liye"},{en:"Because JavaScript engines allow only 5 variables in RAM",hi:"JS engine sirf 5 variables allow karta hai"},{en:"Cleanup is unnecessary because garbage collection handles 100% of event listeners automatically",hi:"Cleanup ki zaroorat nahi hoti"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Unclosed connections and dangling event listeners create references that prevent garbage collection, leading to severe memory leaks over time.",hi:"Dangling listeners aur unclosed connections memory leaks banate hain jo V8 heap ko exhaust karke process crash kar dete hain."}}]};export{e as default};
